<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-LEADING RESULTS OF MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-LEADING RESULTS OF MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING.</headline>
<dateline>KITZBUEHEL, Austria 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times of the</p>
<p>second men's downhill training run in Kitzbuehel on Wednesday,</p>
<p>for Friday's World Cup downhill: 1. Atle Skaardal (Norway) 1</p>
<p>minute 55.78 seconds</p>
<p>2. Luc Alphand (France) 1:55.96</p>
<p>3. Fritz Strobl (Austria) 1:55.98</p>
<p>4. Patrick Ortlieb (Austria) 1:56.27</p>
<p>5. Guenter Mader (Austria) 1:56.34</p>
<p>6. Stefan Krauss (Germany) 1:56.41</p>
<p>7. Peter Runggaldier (Italy) 1:56.59</p>
<p>8. Roland Assinger (Austria) 1:56.64</p>
<p>9. Josef Strobl (Austria) 1:56.76</p>
<p>10. Rob Boyd (Canada) 1:56.95</p>
</text>
